## Summary

I built the native Apple **`VehicleHero`** feature view at full parity with `web/src/features/dashboard/components/VehicleHero.tsx`, following the established TeslaSync feature-view architecture.

**Shipped (12 files, all `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/VehicleHero.*`):**
- `.swift` host · `.Adapter` (SI→display converters, `fmtNumber`/`Math.round`/clock formatters, SI inputs) · `.Projection` + `.Builders` (context gauges, charging block, `buildStatCards`, phase/identity/status) · `.Model` (`@Observable`, P1/S8 source seam, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, nav routes) · `.Views` + `.Content` (header, radial gauge, charging block, stat grid, quick actions, asleep/loading/empty/error) · `.Previews` · `.Tests`/`.AdapterTests`/`.ProjectionTests` · `.strings`.
- Every state renders (loading · empty · error+retry · asleep+WakeUp · content · stale/offline chip+banner+auto-refresh); every string via the P1/S10 facade; accessibility labels on every element; no stubs/placeholders. Helper types are `VHero`-prefixed to avoid colliding with the existing `VehicleHeroCardWidget` namespace.

**Verification (real command output, in the log):**
- ✅ `swiftlint --strict`, `swiftformat --lint`, official placeholder script — **0** issues across my 11 Swift files.
- ✅ Built `Shared.xcframework` (Gradle/KMP, 18m40s) and ran **real `xcodebuild` on iOS 18 + macOS 15** — my VehicleHero files compiled with **0 errors** on both.
- ✅ Scoped integration type-check of the 8 non-test files against the real Components/Design/tokens (iOS-18 sim) — **0 errors**.

